Subject: Cantor Shared Attention and Imagination Runtime P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] bcccafde-5e7c-4ded-a719-2e59ba26369f
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Shared_Attention_Imagination_Runtime_P0.sop

& [Problem] is independent model passes that can exchange prose but cannot inspectably agree on one bounded semantic state or distinguish grounded state from hypothetical exploration

& [Decision] is a pure replicated semantic state machine
  + typed deltas reconcile against one exact predecessor
  + context proxy accounting applies deterministic backpressure
  + frozen same-digest attestations establish a coordination checkpoint
  + DreamFrame contains imagination and emits only a later reviewable proposal

& [Reuse] is intentional
  + SemanticId ContentDigest FacultyKind and canonical SHA-256 machinery already express the required identities
  + ProcedureCoordination proves effectless messaging and replay patterns but is not widened because instruction scheduling and semantic-frame governance have different invariants

& [RejectedAlternative] is direct mid-token hidden-state insertion
  + it couples Cantor to model internals is not transportable across providers and is unnecessary to falsify the semantic coordination hypothesis

& [RejectedAlternative] is consensus as truth
  + correlated models can agree while wrong so sealing records role-bound coordination while epistemic labels evidence and later verification remain independent

& [RejectedAlternative] is unconstrained generative imagination
  + without a sealed parent explicit hypothetical identity forbidden effects evidence requirements and falsifiers generation is indistinguishable from hallucinated authority

& [Value] is one high-leverage seam
  + the same core can later serve local tools llama.cpp passes Codex tasks or distributed faculty machines without changing what a frame delta settlement or dream branch means

& [CostBoundary] is accepted
  + P0 byte accounting is deterministic and testable but not tokenizer exact
  + P0 is an in-memory pure library and does not yet prove transport liveness distributed fault tolerance or model-quality gains
